Z||000000||saleenfiero||08-06-2001||07:13 PM||||Okay, I am very open mided musically.  In my CD changer in the car, I have anything from Mariah Carey to Anthrax to Cypress Hill to George F-ing Michael.  Anyways, I've noticed for years that female song writers seem to be very contrained with the way they write songs.  It seems 99% of the female singers and/or writers today just seem to keep singing about love.  Falling in love, heartbreak, and the like.  I have strived to find 10 women singers who have a song that doesn't involve love of some sort.  I may have found 5.  That's it.  Why is this?  Surely women aren't stupid, I know for a fact that most of them are more level headed and intellectual than all of the guys I know, so why does that gender seem trapped in one song subject?  <P>------------------<BR>'86 SE - My car is actually a MacLaren F1 with a Fiero body kit; or not.||||reg||1
